# CLAUDE.md — {{APP_NAME}}

{{ONE_LINE_DESCRIPTION}} Astro marketing site. Static output · TypeScript
(strictest) · TailwindCSS · bun · Vitest · oxlint + oxfmt + `astro check` ·
deployed to Cloudflare Workers. Read this file first — it is the map and the
rulebook.

## What this repo is (and is not)

This is the **public site**: the pages a stranger and a search crawler see. It is
static HTML, ships almost no JavaScript, and holds no session. The authenticated
product is a **separate repo** (the console app). If a page needs a logged-in
user, it does not belong here.

## Repo map

```
src/pages/         ROUTES — one file per URL. Thin: pick a layout, list sections
src/layouts/       Page shells (<html>, <head>, meta, canonical)
src/sections/      Composed page sections — hero, pricing, faq. One per file
src/ui/            Design-system primitives + globals.css (the ONE stylesheet) + theme/ (palette.css · scale.css · icons.ts)
src/content/       Content collections (markdown)
src/content.config.ts  defineCollection() schemas
src/utilities/     Shared pure helpers
src/constants/     env.ts (Zod-validated), enums
src/types/         Cross-cutting types
public/            Served verbatim at the site root (favicon, robots.txt, og image)
docs/              design-language.md — the house UI rules; read before UI work
astro.config.mjs   Astro config (static output, site URL, Tailwind via vite.plugins)
wrangler.jsonc     Cloudflare Workers deploy config
```

Each `src/*` folder except `pages` has its own `README.md` — read it before
adding files, and add a line when you add something notable.

## Tooling

- Use `bun` for everything (`bun install`, `bun run <script>`, `bunx <bin>`).
- `bun run check` runs the full gate: `astro check` + lint + fmt +
  `check:structure` + `check:unused` (knip) + `check:dupes` (jscpd) + test.
- **`type-check` is `astro check`, not `tsc`.** It is the only tool that
  type-checks an `.astro` file's TEMPLATE body. The split is finer than it
  looks: oxlint **does** read `.astro` frontmatter, so the import and TypeScript
  rules apply there; oxfmt handles `.ts`/`.tsx` (JSX included) but cannot parse
  `.astro` component syntax at all. So a `.astro` file is linted but never
  formatted, and its template body is `astro check`'s job plus review.
- Run `bun run sync` (`astro sync`) after changing `src/content.config.ts`, and
  before `astro check` on a fresh clone — it generates the collection types.
- `bun run dev` starts Astro; `bun run build` produces `dist/`;
  `bunx wrangler dev` serves that build through the real Workers runtime.
- Pre-commit (Lefthook) runs oxlint + oxfmt on staged files.

## Blocked patterns (pre-commit + CI reject these)

- `as any`, `: any`, `as unknown as T` → use `unknown` + type guards.
- `console.log`, `debugger` → use `console.warn` / `console.error`.
- **`axios`** → use `src/utilities/http.ts`. Blocked in lint *and* by the
  structure check reading `package.json`.
- **A hardcoded hex or magic number in a component** → read `--tone-*` custom
  properties so the component works in both bands.
- **`yup` / `valibot` / `joi`, or a hand-written type guard** → `zod`.
- **An `interface` declared beside its schema** → `type X = z.infer<typeof X>`.
- **An unused export, file, or dependency** → knip fails the gate. Delete it.
- **Copy-pasted blocks** → jscpd fails the gate. Extract it.
- **A framework integration used as the default component model** → `.astro`
  components. A React island is for one genuinely interactive section, with a
  comment saying why it can't be static.
- **`client:load` by reflex** → `client:visible` / `client:idle`, or no
  directive at all.
- **Barrel files** (an `index.ts` that only re-exports) → import the concrete file.
- **Default exports** in `.ts` files → named exports. (Config files and
  `.astro` components are exempt; Astro components *are* default exports.)
- **Deep relative imports** (`../../…`) → use the `@/` alias.
- **A page without `title` + `description`** → both are required props on
  `BaseLayout`, because they are product surface, not decoration.
- **Deleting `src/pages/404.astro`** → the structure check fails; `wrangler.jsonc`
  serves it as a real 404 and a soft-200 gets dead URLs indexed.
- **A `<style>` block in a `.astro` file**, a `*.module.css`, a `style` attribute,
  or `styled-components`/`emotion` → Tailwind utilities. `astro check` and oxlint
  both stop at the frontmatter, so this one is on you and the reviewer.
- **`@astrojs/tailwind`** → the deprecated v3 integration; Tailwind is wired as a
  Vite plugin in `astro.config.mjs`. Blocked as a `bannedDep`.
- **`dark:` variants and direct `--color-…` references** → the band is
  class-driven, not OS-driven, and `@theme inline` names emit no variable. Use the
  plain utility (`bg-background`) and let it flip. See `src/ui/theme/palette.css`.
- **Mock-data tests** → tests must exercise real inputs and real integration paths.
- Files over 300 lines (tests exempt) → split.

## Conventions

- **Path alias**: `@/*` → `src/*`. Works in `.astro` frontmatter and `.ts` alike.
- **Filenames**: kebab-case, named after what they are
  (`pricing-section.astro`). One primary export per file.
- **Pages are thin**: a file in `src/pages/` picks a layout and lists sections —
  no markup of its own, no data munging, no styles.
- **Sections own the markup**: one section per file in `src/sections/`. A page
  should read as a list of section names.
- **Static by default**: `output: 'static'`. SSR is a documented, per-page
  decision, not a default. If this project ever turns it on, the reason is
  recorded in Design notes below.
- **Ship no JavaScript you don't need**: Astro sends zero by default. Every
  `client:*` directive is a deliberate choice with a comment.
- **Styling**: **TailwindCSS utilities, always.** `src/ui/globals.css` is the only
  stylesheet on the site — **no Astro scoped `<style>` block**, no CSS Modules, no
  CSS-in-JS, no `style` attribute. The values behind the utilities live in
  `src/ui/theme/palette.css` (what swaps per band) and `scale.css` (what never
  swaps). Type is applied by role — `type-display`, `type-body`, `type-marker` —
  never by picking a size.
- **Validation**: `zod` at every boundary — env, anything the build fetches,
  content-collection schemas — and the TypeScript type comes from `z.infer`,
  never declared alongside the schema. Inside `src/content.config.ts` use
  `astro/zod` (Astro's re-export, so collection types are generated correctly);
  everywhere else import `zod` directly. Same library, one convention.
- **Testing**: co-locate tests in a sibling `__tests__/`, real data only.
- **Doc line required**: every module and public symbol carries a concise
  `/** … */` doc line; `.astro` components carry one in their frontmatter.
- **Docs in sync**: a change to a user-facing surface updates the prose
  describing it (README, the relevant `src/*/README.md`, `CLAUDE.md`) in the
  **same** change.
- **Commits**: `type(scope): description` (conventional). Push to feature
  branches; never directly to main.

## Guard rails

Four layers, and none of them are optional:

1. **These rules**, read first by every agent working here.
2. **Pre-commit** (Lefthook) — oxlint + oxfmt on staged files.
3. **CI** (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) — the whole gate plus a production build,
   each check its own named step.
4. **AI code review** (`.github/workflows/code-review.yml`) — reviews every PR
   against this file, read from the base branch.

Never advance while any of them is red, **even on an unrelated failure**. Fix it
or say plainly that it is broken; do not disable a check to get green.

## Design notes

<!-- The setup design-context answers are recorded here: audience, tone, palette
direction. The token stylesheets (src/ui/theme/*.css) hold the concrete values. -->

> **Before any UI work, read [`docs/design-language.md`](./docs/design-language.md)** —
> the full house language (bands, signal, type, motion, glyphs, contrast gate,
> banned list, and a self-check). It is deliberately not summarised here: this
> file loads every session, that one loads only when you touch UI.

This site shares its token set with the console app **on purpose** — they are one
product, and a visitor who signs up should not feel a seam. If a token changes
here, it changes there too.

The site follows the house **CodaSignal "Signal"** design language: full-bleed
bands that alternate dark (`#0e0f0d`) and light (`#f2f2ee`) with a quarter-width
ruled backdrop behind each, one chromatic signal in four temperatures (Jade is
the default) that only ever marks the second line of a heading, live data, or a
list number, Archivo at 600/500 with tight negative tracking for everything
readable, and JetBrains Mono for every label/tag/data/glyph line. Depth is a
hairline. No serif, no italic, no second hue, no gradients, no icon library.

**Hard rules:** no hardcoded hex or magic numbers in sections — utilities only.
The token stylesheets reset Tailwind's stock scales to `initial`, so `text-sm`,
`font-bold`, `rounded-2xl`, `shadow-lg`, `ease-in-out` and the stock colour ramps
do not exist here; that is the ban being structural, not a class that failed to
load. The signal never fills a button. Focus is always visible. Motion flattens
under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`. The band is a CSS-variable seam: `:root`
carries the dark band, `.band-light` overrides it, and the utilities resolve
through `var(--tone-*)` — so a section follows whichever band it lands in, as
long as it never hardcodes a value.

- **Deviations from the house language:** <none | what-and-why>

